6. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

Implement security as part of the architecture.

Required controls include:

Authentication:
- secure password hashing
- no plaintext passwords
- secure authentication
- appropriate session/token handling
- login failure handling

Authorization:
- server-side RBAC
- method/endpoint-level authorization
- least privilege
- supervisor-only signal modification
- administrator-only user/sensor administration

Input validation:
- validate request DTOs
- validate ranges
- reject malformed requests
- validate signal configuration
- validate emergency requests
- validate sensor readings

Secure errors:
- never expose stack traces
- never expose passwords/secrets
- never expose unnecessary database details
- use centralized exception handling

Audit:
Log security-sensitive actions such as:
- login success/failure
- role changes
- signal configuration changes
- emergency priority requests
- sensor registration
- unauthorized requests
- important incident changes

Availability:
- request validation
- request-size controls
- rate limiting where practical
- protection against excessive requests

Secrets:
- NEVER hard-code passwords
- NEVER hard-code API keys
- NEVER commit database passwords
- NEVER commit tokens
- use environment variables / configuration / Kubernetes Secrets where appropriate

Database:
- use least-privilege application credentials
- use parameterized queries/JPA
- do not create SQL injection vulnerabilities intentionally

